```
func ValidatePersistentVolumeClaimUpdate(newPvc, oldPvc *core.PersistentVolumeClaim) field.ErrorList {
	allErrs := ValidateObjectMetaUpdate(...)
	allErrs = append(allErrs, ValidatePersistentVolumeClaim(newPvc)...)
	newPvcClone := newPvc.DeepCopy()
	oldPvcClone := oldPvc.DeepCopy()
	// PVController needs to update PVC status. It is possible for a PVC to be missing...
	if utilfeature.DefaultFeatureGate.Enabled(features.ExpandPersistentVolumes) {
		if newPvcClone.Spec.Resources.Requests == nil {
			newPvcClone.Spec.Resources.Requests = v1.ResourceList{}
		}
		...
	}
	allErrs = append(allErrs, ValidateImmutableField(newPvcClone.Spec, oldPvcClone.Spec, field.NewPath("spec"))...)
```

Hmm, there's `ValidateImmutableField(newPvcClone.Spec, oldPvcClone.Spec...)` after normalize, meaning spec immutable entirely except what's normalized (resources.requests, VolumeAttributesClassName maybe). Actually volumeName got special handling? Let me just test with dry-run=server. If patch is rejected, we know.

